==Spanish==

===Etymology===
Uncertain. Possibly related to Italian {{term|puttana|lang=it}} (Old Spanish ''[[putaña]]''; see ''[[putañear]]''), which ultimately derives from {{etyl|la|es}} {{term|putus||pure|lang=la}}. María Moliner dictionary (also Joan Coromines<ref>[[w:en:Joan Coromines|Joan Coromines]], ''Breve diccionario etimológico de la lengua castellana'', tercera edición 2011, ISBN 978-84-249-0374-9</ref>) states the most probable origin: from {{etyl|VL.|es}}  {{term|putta|lang=la}}, variant of {{term|puta|lang=la}}, female form of {{term|puttus|lang=la}}, {{term|putus||boy|lang=la}}. Note that this word appears in all romance languages.

